predicate. No merge, deployment, issue closure or whole-renderer acceptance is claimed.\r\n\r\nReview this exact head: `50e46b7ecfde9c8bea9c0cf00b6017afaf27aab9` (parent reviewed head `f0647b44e10c9ce4f80895b52861893c347512fd`). Main remains `18ff14860ff41c084b1db5f396bb62aa9c22b1be`. Current runtime SHA-256: `040192b555fa0db2fad760470ec020a06d86d3e0c7615153062ec5e76c50a2d5`. Root entry SHA-256: `67e2ff84eb1e7422bfc390f98b641c8e3f93f76a77400401681be10676eb8d3d`.\r\n\r\nThe [revision record](https://github.com/theislampill/salah_widget/blob/50e46b7ecfde9c8bea9c0cf00b6017afaf27aab9/docs/real-sky/PR43_REVIEW_REVISION.md) and [portable evidence index](https://github.com/theislampill/salah_widget/blob/50e46b7ecfde9c8bea9c0cf00b6017afaf27aab9/docs/real-sky/pr43-review-evidence/README.md) contain the controls, captures, exact inventories, independent readbacks and remaining limits.\r\n\r\n- R1: native core has its own closing script boundary before full refinement. A compact receiver derived from the same initial V5 inputs composes the early Moon and catalogue together through the native phase/geometry/presentation owners. Entry size falls from 6,082,431 decoded / 4,271,135 gzip bytes to 1,544,863 / 809,338. The 549,170-byte compact payload and its 815,849-byte head script still precede core boot; the dependency is reduced, not eliminated. No longer loader, hidden card, delayed Moon substitution or new provider wait was added.\r\n- Initial receiver fields are quantized, not lossless copies. Forty sampled full-V5 comparisons retain the original RMS≤4/255, p95≤12/255 and silhouette≤0.5 device-pixel gates; maximum RMS 2.410503/255, p95 4/255, coverage mismatch 0. Localized maximum error 68/255 remains disclosed. Full terrain/material/kernel assets are unchanged. Independent decoder review confirms exact decoded-byte and rejection behavior.\r\n- R2: registered Fraunces/Inter face identity/status and individual face settlement invalidate the cached fit. Stable missing/failed fonts retain fallback fitting; typography remains nonblocking. Natural test paths do not clear the cache or call fitting manually.\r\n\r\nValidation binds the generated runtime above:\r\n\r\n- Both engines fail the reviewed actual-entry held-tail executable control and pass the corrected control. Current04 adds 12 day/night held-tail/core/compressed cases: eight causal controls pass and four transfer observations complete without page errors. Actual settings actions and all six prayer rows are checked. Both held-run final captures reach current refined terrain; held durations are not ordinary performance qualification.\r\n- Current typography: 18 actual-widget cases, nine each in Windows Chromium148 and Firefox150, pass scoped checks for delayed CSS/bytes, successful arrival, permanent failure, warm entry, long prayer names and split-face arrival. The original/corrected 36-case packet and the intermediate split-face failure remain retained. Broader layout/access/calendar work is separate.\r\n- Six current ordinary source-frame captures yield **five strict FAIL / one Firefox new-document PASS**, with unchanged S1 budgets. Earlier exact-main captures are explicitly reused rather than presented as fresh matched runs. Source-frame receipts, original images and viewing clips are distinguished; no physical-monitor or actual-extension-parent claim is made.\r\n- Two disposable builds agree, all 141 served runtime files are bound, V1 verifies, and generated outputs are copied exactly. Focused source checks retain 386 distinct passing assertions/tests and four inherited TODOs; decoder-only reruns are not counted as new distinct tests. Original failed fixtures and controls remain in the packet.\r\n\r\nThe existing 213-node/409-edge DAG retains R1/R2 as required inputs to affected active nodes. S1/callback/actual-parent work, R0022-L1 display repair and S10 acceptance remain open and separate. Completed spotlight attribution is reused. Mac/Apple Bash 3.2 remains owner-deferred. Weather provenance, prayer/settings authority, approved body size, Earthshine, opacity, catalogue, V5 and frozen V1 are preserved within the documented source/evidence boundaries.\r\n\r\nRefs #33, #34, #25. Historical qualification below the amended documents remains historical; this packet grants no RLGWO closure certificate.\r\n","created_at":"2026-10-09T05:28:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T09:38:28Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"bd2e7e685d240f74da4b986366469938f7f10ba4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theislampill/salah_widget/pulls/43/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theislampill/salah_widget/pulls/43/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theislampill/salah_widget/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theislampill/salah_widget/issues/43/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theislampill/salah_widget/statuses/50e46b7ecfde9c8bea9c0cf00b6017afaf27aab9","head":{"label":"theislampill:codex/celestial-startup-repair","ref":"codex/celestial-startup-repair","sha":"50e46b7ecfde9c8bea9c0cf00b6017afaf27aab9","user":{"login":"theislampill","id":266501826,"node_id":"U_kgDOD-J-wg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266501826?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/theislampill","html_url":"https://github.com/theislampill","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theislampill/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theislampill/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theislampill/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theislampill/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theislampill/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theislampill/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users